// An INT literal in a float constructor converts (t_dc1d92b0).
//
// `float4(1,1,1,1)` is the most idiomatic constant in Cg and it did not
// build.  The IR builder's constructor fold only accepted float
// constants, so one int literal stopped the whole constructor folding;
// the back end then saw four loose constants instead of a literal vec4
// and every matcher that wants one refused:
//
//     nv40-fp: StoreOutput source is not a direct varying input, tex2D
//     result, or literal vec4 (arithmetic lowering lands later)
//
// An honest refusal rather than a miscompile, which is why this is not a
// P1 - but the reference compiles all of these, and so should we.  The
// second fixture covers the other spelling, an int-initialised float
// VARIABLE, which turned out to be the same site.
void main(out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    oColor = float4(1, 1, 1, 1);
}
